  "rationale": "The 50 MSPS throughput constraint forces 1 result/cycle (pipelined or pipelined_m) or a high-Fmax unrolled_k; the iterative family (1 result every N+3 cycles) cannot plausibly reach 50 MSPS and is excluded. The accuracy constraint (max_abs_err <= 2^-12) is met by modest n_iter (~12-14) with rounding, so I bound data_width 14-20 and n_iter 12-18 to focus the search on the feasible region where the power/accuracy trade-off actually lives, rather than wasting budget on over-accurate or infeasible corners. I weight pipelined (0.5) and pipelined_m (0.3) as the primary throughput-capable families, and keep unrolled_k (0.2) as a power challenger. angle_guard 0-2 and frac_guard 0-2 keep the datapath narrow to minimise power while preserving accuracy headroom; rounding is left to the optimizer to find the trunc/round boundary. This spreads the 400-eval budget across the families most likely to populate the Pareto front."
